Hi George,
If you have ties in your data (e.g., control individuals with the same propensity score) you might get slightly different matches each time, depending on which matching method you are using.  (If there are ties, some of the matching methods will select the match randomly).  You can use the set.seed() command at the beginning to set the random seed, which should then lead to the same matches each time.

Liz


